			<div class="content" id="post-content-2164696">
									

<p>The best explanation I can give is through this conversation I had with Reach. Note that the following can be considered spoilers, but shouldn't be considered the truth of what's going on in this article.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&lt;Reach|Review&gt; I started thinking, by the way, that the friggin' attic didn't even exist.<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; Good.<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; Let me background a bit<br />
&lt;Reach|Review&gt; Go fer it!<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; I had a brother who died when I was little. He was a newborn, but he didn't make it.<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; Really shook the family up<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; I didn't handle it well at the time<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; and even though I never met him, I kept seeing him everywhere<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; anyway<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; in the dream, he's in the attic.<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; And I dont realize it until the very end<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; but then I find that he never existed<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; So, yeah.<br />
&lt;kaktus&gt; That's basically what's going on here.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, many thanks to Reach, TwistedGears, Roget, and others who looked at this. It feels good to write this one, I hope you guys like it.</p>
<p>As usual, your comments, critiques and criticisms are always welcome.</p>

